criteria:
Inclusion Criteria:

* age ≥18 years;
* histologically confirmed pT1 urothelial carcinoma of the bladder (any grade, WHO 2022 and 1973 classifications) on the definitive histology of the initial TURBt;
* macroscopically complete initial resection as reported by the surgeon, with detrusor muscle present in the specimen, both formally documented in the operative and pathology records;
* indication for second TURBt according to EAU guidelines, with the procedure scheduled at the study centre and expected within ten weeks of the initial TURBt;
* clinically localised non-metastatic disease (cN0, cM0);
* patients able to provide written informed consent.
* Previous BCG treatment is allowed.

Exclusion Criteria:

* muscle-invasive disease (≥pT2) on the definitive histology of the initial TURBt;
* initial resection judged incomplete by the operating surgeon - whether because visible tumour was deliberately left behind or because the procedure had to be curtailed and a planned second look arranged - or absence of detrusor muscle in the specimen - these patients receive second TURBt per guidelines but are outside the study question, which concerns the completely resected patient;
* pure non-urothelial histology (primary adenocarcinoma, pure squamous cell carcinoma, small cell neuroendocrine carcinoma, sarcoma). Variant histologies of urothelial carcinoma are not an exclusion criterion but are recorded as a covariate;
* concomitant upper tract urothelial carcinoma, or a history of it within the preceding 24 months, given the documented positivity of Bladder EpiCheck® in that disease \[19\];
* A single early post-operative chemotherapy instillation, where given, is not an exclusion criterion but is recorded as a covariate;
* previous pelvic radiotherapy;
* indwelling urinary catheter or intermittent self-catheterisation; urinary diversion or neobladder;
* clinically non-localised disease (cN+, cM+);
* pregnancy or breastfeeding;
* TURBt performed in an emergency setting for uncontrolled bleeding or other life-threatening indication, in which resection quality cannot be assured;
* second TURBt not performed at the study centre, with consequent unavailability of the reference standard;
* patients unable to provide written informed consent, or any condition that in the investigator's judgement compromises the ability to comply with study procedures.
